 This file is generated from ELWDCTEL.MST by TOOLS\MKMSG.PY.  Edit the
 template, not this file, when changing the module's source.

 Settings are not in this file.  Change them online: in Teleconference,
 a Sysop types DICE SET.  Changes take effect immediately.


LEVEL6 {Dice for Teleconference}

 DICE FOR TELECONFERENCE - TEXT

 Values in these messages are named text variables, DCT_xxx, so you
 can reword or reorder the text freely.

HELP {<ESC>[0;1;36mDice <ESC>[0;36mversion <TV:DCT_VERSION>
<ESC>[1;37m<TV:DCT_DICE> ON<ESC>[0;36m     lets you roll dice with <ESC>[1;37m<TV:DCT_ROLL><ESC>[0;36m
<ESC>[1;37m<TV:DCT_DICE> OFF<ESC>[0;36m    turns dice rolling off again
<ESC>[1;37m<TV:DCT_ROLL> <ESC>[33m[n]D[sides]<ESC>[0;36m  rolls n dice with that many sides
<ESC>[0;36mUp to <TV:DCT_MAXN> dice, with up to <TV:DCT_MAXS> sides.  Everyone in the channel sees the roll.
<ESC>[0;36mExamples:  <ESC>[1;37m<TV:DCT_ROLL> D20<ESC>[0;36m   <ESC>[1;37m<TV:DCT_ROLL> 3D8<ESC>[0;36m   <ESC>[1;37m<TV:DCT_ROLL> 4<ESC>[0;36m (four six-sided dice)
} T Dice: help

DICEON {<ESC>[0;1;32mDice rolling is on.  Roll with <TV:DCT_ROLL>; type <TV:DCT_DICE> HELP for how.
} T Dice: turned on

DICEOFF {<ESC>[0;1;32mDice rolling is off.  Type <TV:DCT_DICE> ON to turn it back on.
} T Dice: turned off

ISOFF {<ESC>[0;1;33mDice rolling is off for you.  Type <TV:DCT_DICE> ON first.
} T Dice: ROLL used while off

BADFMT {<ESC>[0;1;33mI can't read that.  Try <TV:DCT_ROLL> 3D8, <TV:DCT_ROLL> D20 or <TV:DCT_ROLL> 4.  Type <TV:DCT_DICE> HELP for help.
} T Dice: could not read the roll

BADN {<ESC>[0;1;33mSorry, you can only roll between 1 and <TV:DCT_MAXN> dice at a time.  Type <TV:DCT_DICE> HELP for more help.
} T Dice: too many or too few dice

BADSIDES {<ESC>[0;1;33mSorry, dice must have between 2 and <TV:DCT_MAXS> sides.  Type <TV:DCT_DICE> HELP for more help.
} T Dice: too many or too few sides

 What the person who rolled sees.  DCT_NDICE and DCT_SIDES are the
 count and sides, DCT_ROLLS the list of results ("4, 2 and 6"), and
 DCT_TOTAL the sum.

ME1 {<ESC>[0;1;35mYou roll a <ESC>[1m<TV:DCT_SIDES><ESC>[0;1;35m-sided die and get a <ESC>[1;36m<TV:DCT_TOTAL><ESC>[0;1;35m.<ESC>[0m
} T Dice: you rolled one die

MEN {<ESC>[0;1;35mYou roll <ESC>[1m<TV:DCT_NDICE> <TV:DCT_SIDES><ESC>[0;1;35m-sided dice and get <ESC>[1;36m<TV:DCT_ROLLS><ESC>[0;1;35m (for a total of <ESC>[1m<TV:DCT_TOTAL><ESC>[0;1;35m).<ESC>[0m
} T Dice: you rolled several dice

MENT {<ESC>[0;1;35mYou roll <ESC>[1m<TV:DCT_NDICE> <TV:DCT_SIDES><ESC>[0;1;35m-sided dice for a total of <ESC>[1;36m<TV:DCT_TOTAL><ESC>[0;1;35m.<ESC>[0m
} T Dice: you rolled so many that the list is left out

 The line everyone else in the channel sees, on this board and on
 boards linked through MajorLink.  Teleconference shows it as ordinary
 chat from the person who rolled, so it appears after "From <user>:".
 Keep each to one line, and plain text: other boards may not show
 colors the way yours does.

PUB1 {[Dice] rolls a <TV:DCT_SIDES>-sided die and gets a <TV:DCT_TOTAL>.} T Dice: line for the channel, one die

PUBN {[Dice] rolls <TV:DCT_NDICE> <TV:DCT_SIDES>-sided dice and gets <TV:DCT_ROLLS> (for a total of <TV:DCT_TOTAL>).} T Dice: line for the channel, several dice

PUBNT {[Dice] rolls <TV:DCT_NDICE> <TV:DCT_SIDES>-sided dice for a total of <TV:DCT_TOTAL>.} T Dice: line for the channel, list left out

RESTING {<ESC>[0;1;33mThe dice are put away right now.  Try again later.
} T Dice: turned off by the Sysop

NOACCESS {<ESC>[0;1;31mSorry, you don't have access to the dice.
} T Dice: no access

SQUELCH {<ESC>[0;1;31mYou can't roll dice while you are squelched.
} T Dice: user is squelched

NOCHAN {<ESC>[0;1;33mThe dice aren't available in <TV:DCT_CHANNEL>.
} T Dice: not allowed in this channel

 The Sysop's settings editor: DICE SET.

SETHDR {<ESC>[0;1;36mDice for Teleconference <TV:DCT_VERSION> - settings
} T Dice settings: heading

SETROW {<ESC>[0;1;33m<TV:DCT_SETNUM:R:2>. <ESC>[37m<TV:DCT_SETNAME>: <ESC>[32m<TV:DCT_SETVALUE>
} T Dice settings: one setting

SETFOOT {<ESC>[0;36mChange one: <ESC>[1;37m<TV:DCT_DICE> SET <ESC>[33m<number> <value>
<ESC>[0;36mAll back to the defaults: <ESC>[1;37m<TV:DCT_DICE> SET DEFAULTS
} T Dice settings: how to change them

SETOK {<ESC>[0;1;32m<TV:DCT_SETNAME> is now <ESC>[37m<TV:DCT_SETVALUE><ESC>[32m.
} T Dice settings: changed

SETBAD {<ESC>[0;1;31m<TV:DCT_SETNAME> needs <TV:DCT_SETRANGE>.
<ESC>[0;36mIt is still <ESC>[1;37m<TV:DCT_SETVALUE><ESC>[0;36m.
} T Dice settings: value not accepted

SETDEF {<ESC>[0;1;32mEvery dice setting is back to its default.
} T Dice settings: reset
